12510 def proc calc_ysize (y_csize%)
12520 rem This tries to calculate the window y size depending on the given y size,
12530 rem the number of rows wished in the menu appsub window and the y position of
12540 rem the menu appsub window.
12550 rem It uses and changes the GLOBAL variables rows%, app_y_orig% and ysize%.
12560 rem It also uses the GLOBAL var maxy% which is the maximum y size a window
12570 rem could have in the current screen resolution.
12580 rem algo is as follows:
12590 rem if both ysize and rows% are undefined (=-1) : make wdw as big as possible
12600 rem if one is undefined, calc the other
12610 rem if both are defined, give precedence to the rows number
12620 rem
12630 rem param : y_csize% is the y character height, either 0 (10 pix) or 1 (20 pix)
12640 rem
12650 local y_spcg%
12660   if rows%=0:return
12670   y_spcg% = 12+(y_csize%*10)
12680   if rows%= -1
12690     if ysize%= -1
12700       rows%=(maxy%-14-app_y_orig%) div y_spcg% : rem max nbr of rows
12710     else
12720       rows%= (ysize%-app_y_orig%-4) div y_spcg%
12730     endif
12740   endif
12750   if rows%<2:rows%=2
12760   ysize%=rows%*y_spcg%+app_y_orig%+4
12770   if ysize%>=maxy%-14
12780     ysize%=maxy%-app_y_orig%-14
12790     rows%=ysize% div y_spcg%
12800     ysize%=rows%*y_spcg% + app_y_orig% + 4
12810   endif
12820   if ysize%<minysize%
12830     ysize%=minysize% -app_y_orig%-14
12840     rows%=ysize% div y_spcg%
12850     ysize%=rows%*y_spcg% + app_y_orig% + 4
12860   endif
12870 end def calc_ysize
